1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,975
A cloud estate is more than a bill.

2
00:00:03,135 --> 00:00:07,485
Someone still has to investigate, propose, and decide.

3
00:00:08,005 --> 00:00:18,405
Flexera's 2025 State of the Cloud report says managing cloud spend is the top challenge for eighty-four percent of organizations.

4
00:00:18,565 --> 00:00:25,240
The bill, the inventory, and the recommendation still sit apart from the person who has to act.

5
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:28,510
Infralens is one product.

6
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:36,345
The console holds the estate. The agentic side works the same project. There is no second suite.

7
00:00:36,865 --> 00:00:38,915
Open the estate.

8
00:00:39,075 --> 00:00:48,650
The dashboard reads a saved snapshot of cost, resources, alerts, and Advisor, and only for the subscriptions on this project.

9
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:54,570
In chat, Agent runs a skill. Plan returns steps you can execute.

10
00:00:54,730 --> 00:01:03,630
The default scope is read-only. The agent analyses and recommends. It does not pretend a live change already happened.

11
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:16,065
Workflows enqueue a run when Azure or AWS is connected and the worker is up. Findings from those runs stay open, with the gate and the recommended action.

12
00:01:16,585 --> 00:01:22,485
Architecture keeps a Solution Architect run, and the stage of that delivery.

13
00:01:22,645 --> 00:01:30,395
You take a change into chat. Approval records the decision. The approvals inbox does not execute it.

14
00:01:30,915 --> 00:01:35,490
The result is one project for the estate and for the agent.

15
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:41,475
A person is still accountable before Azure or AWS is changed.

16
00:01:41,995 --> 00:01:47,495
Infralens. See the estate. Ask the agent. Decide before you change it.
